 "notes": "SCGS OFR-27 (Bynum, 1983), geologic map of the southern half of the Ware Shoals West quadrangle (Old Saluda copper mine area), 1:24,000. Map symbols read from the legend image; the text recognition misread several of them ('6D' for GD, '(ETF)' for BIF, '4A' for AA, 'FL' for FI, 'G6' for GG) and missed EQG and BG. No ages or descriptions printed. Strike and dip values of compositional layering and the plunging anticline and syncline symbols are many and not itemized; section line A-A' is drawn but no section is on the sheet; mine symbols not itemized. Drill holes DDH 5, 6 and 7 read from the map face (location note is general). SUBSURFACE: none.",
